      "writtenOn": "2025-08-01T14:19:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e This call successfully adds a label definition to the project.\n\nThis is hard to follow.\n\n`LabelType globalLabelType \u003d `\n\nHere we set some values for `1, 0, -1`\n\nThen we pass different values for `1` here\n\nFrom `Approved` to `LGTM`\n\nThat does not matter here?  \n\n```\n    LabelType globalLabelType \u003d\n        LabelType.builder(\n                \"Global-Label\",\n                ImmutableList.of(\n                    LabelValue.create((short) 1, \"Approved\"),\n                    LabelValue.create((short) 0, \"No vote\"),\n                    LabelValue.create((short) -1, \"Rejected\")))\n            .setDescription(\"A global label\")\n            .setFunction(LabelFunction.NO_OP)\n            .setCanOverride(false)\n            .build();\n```\n\nThis only creates a label without adding to `project`?\n\n`configLabel(` adds the actual `label` to the `project`?\n\nSo where do we attempt to actually override this label?",
      "parentUuid": "9b0e3533_3d871b87",
