      "writtenOn": "2025-08-04T06:41:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Label definitions are inherited. To find the label definitions for a project that directly inherits from All-Projects we read:\n\n1. global label definitions provided by the new extension point\n2. labels defined in All-Projects\n3. labels defined in the project itself\n\nWith this test we add a label definition for a label called \"Global-Label\" at 1. (label defined at l. 83 - 93 and registered at l. 106) and at 3. (l. 96 - 104).\n\nA label definition at a lower level override the inherited label definition if it has the same name. So the label definition for \"Global-Label\" at 3. overrides the inherited \"Global-Label\" that was defined at 1., but only if the label definition at 1. has canOverride set to true.\n\nThe override at 3. attempts to redefine the label with different voting values and the assertion checks that this didn\u0027t work and the voting values from the global label still apply (because the override is not allowed and the label definition at 3. gets ignored).\n\nSo the label definition at 3. matters for the test, because the test is verifying that this label definition gets ignored. The label definition at 3. must have the same name as the label definition at 1. and it must differ by at least one property so that we can verify which label definition was taken (for that we modified the voting values).\n\nContext:\nDisallowing to override labels, does not prevent adding label definitions with the same name at a lower level, but if they are added, or pre-exist, they are simply ignored. If we wouldn\u0027t ignore these label definitions, each time a non-overridable label is added (or an existing label is made non-overridable) at a higher level, we would need to scan through all projects on lower levels to find and remove label definitions with the same name, e.g we would need to scan all projects if a label in All-Projects becomes non-overridable. Doing this is too expensive and non-atomic, hence we don\u0027t do that and we just allow potentially overriding label definitions to exist and then just ignore them if needed.",
      "parentUuid": "b7e0bbf7_781e6126",
